  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/8d31dc0c38fbd5f1b3a39a53d3d50939421509ddcef45a96e56d2aa367ed4cd8.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡D=$",
  "worked_solution": "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to the angle $D,$ the opposite side is $\\overset{―}{BC},$ and the adjacent is $\\overset{―}{BD}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡D & =\\frac{BC}{BD} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
